h it (e.g. a parity test), since JIRA_UPDATE_FIELDS does not currently exist.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search for 'JIRA_UPDATE_FIELDS' across the repo returns (no matches)","dispatch_apply_phases.py:73: _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST = frozenset({'summary','description','assignee','priority','status'})","Plan 'Approach': 'compute the survival test in differ.py from the shared JIRA_UPDATE_FIELDS constant in _field_contract.py'"],"finding":"The Approach says to 'compute the survival test in differ.py from the shared JIRA_UPDATE_FIELDS constant in _field_contract.py (no batch_dispatch import)', but no JIRA_UPDATE_FIELDS constant exists in _field_contract.py. The actual Jira-update allowlist is _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST = frozenset({'summary','description','assignee','priority','status'}) defined in dispatch_apply_phases.py:73. The plan thus silently requires creating a new constant that duplicates and must stay in sync with the real allowlist — a coupling the differ currently avoids — without naming the source of truth or a parity mechanism.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f051a174f49272083","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Approach'; _field_contract.py / dispatch_apply_phases.py:73","norm_id":"n8d0c4f2ecd5c4582","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The allowlist changes in dispatch_apply_phases.py (e.g. a field added) but the new _field_contract.JIRA_UPDATE_FIELDS is not updated, silently re-inflating or over-suppressing branch-3 emits"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is